    "reply": "I reviewed `shop/payments.py` and wrote the findings to `REVIEW.md` at the repo root. The verdict is **REQUEST CHANGES**. The main problem is that money is handled with floats, and `refund` has no bounds checks. No tests exist for the module.\n\nThe blockers are:\n- **Float money math** (lines 3, 7, 15): the tax rate and all totals use `float`. `round(..., 2)` also uses banker's rounding, so totals can be a cent off.\n- **`refund` has no validation** (lines 18\u201319): negative amounts, refunds larger than the order total, and unrounded results all pass through.\n\nThe major items are missing input validation in `line_total` and `order_total`, and no tests for the module. I also flagged that tax is applied to the whole subtotal rather than per line, which the author should confirm against the tax rules. I didn't modify any source files.",
